Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"inflection_curve_start":"2026-03-15","peak":"Apr-Jul (flamingo breeding, ~40,000 birds)","fire_date":"2026-03-01","shoulder":"Aug-Oct (green/rainy)","booking_lead_weeks":"4-8","notes":"Río Lagartos flamingos peak Apr-Sep (breeding) — OPPOSITE window to Celestún (Nov-Mar). Follow-the-sun within Yucatán. Las Coloradas pinkest Mar + Jul-Aug. Sharpen on live tracking."},"jewels":[{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Flamingo boat safari (Ría Lagartos)","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.getyourguide.com/rio-lagartos-l146496/ttd/","si":"expedition","commission":"DMC (Amstar) / GetYourGuide-Viator affiliate"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Las Coloradas pink lakes (no swim)","tier":"essential","source":"https://travelbooksfood.com/las-coloradas-pink-lakes-of-mexico-yucatan","timing":"Apr-Jul","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Apr-Jul","commission":"activity affiliate + non-commissionable entry pass-through"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Crocodile night tour","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g1168987-d1965637-Reviews-Rio_Lagartos_Adventures-Rio_Lagartos_Yucatan_Peninsula.html","timing":"Apr-Jul","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Apr-Jul","commission":"DMC / cooperative referral"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Mayan mud bath (Baño Maya)","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g1168987-d1965637-Reviews-Rio_Lagartos_Adventures-Rio_Lagartos_Yucatan_Peninsula.html","timing":"Apr-Jul","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Apr-Jul","commission":"bundled in boat tour"},{"si_tag":"tropical","name":"San Felipe fishing village","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.letstraveltomexico.com/rio-lagartos-yucatan/","timing":"Apr-Jul","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"tropical","when":"Apr-Jul","commission":"content halo → dining/lodging affiliate"},{"si_tag":"tropical","name":"El Cuyo kite / quiet beach","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.letstraveltomexico.com/el-cuyo-yucatan/","timing":"Apr-Jul","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"tropical","when":"Apr-Jul","commission":"kite-school + guesthouse affiliate/bedbank"}],"faq":[{"q":"When is the best time to see flamingos at Río Lagartos?","a":"April through July, the breeding concentration, when counts reach near 40,000 birds — the exact opposite window from Celestún, which peaks November–March. Counts swing year to year with water level and salinity, so book the reserve and the season, not a promised number, and sharpen on live tracking before committing to a date.","source":"letstraveltomexico.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Can you swim in the Las Coloradas pink lakes?","a":"Default no — plan for it. Las Coloradas is a working industrial hypersaline salt operation (Mexico''s #2), not a swim beach; entry is rule-bound and guide-mandatory, and drones are banned by the salt company. A 2026 report suggests a limited, pre-booked 10-minute swim window may again be permitted at specific spots, but treat that as unconfirmed and volatile and default to the no-swim expectation.","source":"travelbooksfood.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What else will I see besides flamingos?","a":"A full biosphere: 400+ logged bird species, crocodiles on the after-dark night run (mellow and family-friendly for older kids), the white halophilic-clay \"Baño Maya\" mud bath, and the salt-flat geology behind the pink. The reserve is a dedicated birding vertical once the Wildlife SI opens.","source":"tripadvisor.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"wildlife"},{"q":"Is there a beach at Río Lagartos?","a":"Yes — three quiet ones. Cancunito is a white-sand swim beach near town, San Felipe (12 km west) is a pastel fishing village with fresh seafood, and El Cuyo (45 min east) is a resort-free barrier-beach village inside the biosphere with steady side-shore wind for kitesurfing, peaking Dec–Feb.","source":"letstraveltomexico.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Río Lagartos?","a":"Distance to trauma care, not crime. The town has only a basic clinic; Tizimín is ~1 hr, Valladolid''s hospital ~1.5 hr (with 24-hr ambulance transfer for serious cases), and Mérida''s full private hospitals ~2–2.5 hr. Serious injury means a long road transfer, so build the medevac distance into expectations, especially for older travelers, and carry insurance.","source":"yucatanmagazine.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Río Lagartos & Las Coloradas: Flamingos and Pink Lakes | TravelWell.World","search_language":"en","local_keywords":["flamencos Río Lagartos","Las Coloradas Yucatán","reserva de la biosfera Ría Lagartos","tour flamencos Yucatán","baño Maya Río Lagartos","El Cuyo kitesurf"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-06"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["expedition","tropical"],"ultra":[{"name":"Chablé Yucatán","type":"Mérida luxury hacienda base (hub-and-spoke)","distance":"~25 min from Mérida; day-trip flamingos","earning_lane":"Fora advisor lane","tier":"ULTRA","note":"No branded ultra on the flamingo coast; luxury = hacienda base + private CONANP charter"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Río Lagartos, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":21.5983,"lng":-88.1592}}'::jsonb, 91)
