against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":["Nov-Apr dry season","Dia de Muertos (Oct 31-Nov 2)","Semana Santa (2026: Mar 29-Apr 5)"],"inflection":"6-10 weeks pre-peak; boutique tier sells 8-12 weeks out","fire_date":"curve-start minus 1-2 weeks (dry-season fire ~mid-Sep; Dia de Muertos fire ~early-mid Oct; Semana Santa 2026 fire ~early-mid Mar) — proceeds with mandatory L3 disclosure","off_season":"May-Oct green/rainy value window; culture fully accessible year-round; highland climate never hot"},"jewels":[{"name":"Andadores + Templo de Santo Domingo + Museo del Ámbar","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://randomtrip.net/san-cristobal-de-las-casas-travel-guide-chiapas-mexico/","timing":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","commission":"city walking tour + hotel + shopping affiliate (live behind BWW)"},{"name":"San Juan Chamula syncretic church","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://bucketlistbri.com/san-juan-chamula-chiapas-mexico/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","when":"year-round","commission":"guided community day tour ~US$65pp (live); community fee non-commissionable"},{"name":"Zinacantán weaving co-op","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://bucketlistbri.com/zinacantan-mexico/","timing":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","commission":"Chamula+Zinacantán combo tour + co-op purchase (live)"},{"name":"Kakaw Museo del Cacao + café/chocolate culture","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://randomtrip.net/san-cristobal-de-las-casas-travel-guide-chiapas-mexico/","timing":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","commission":"food/cultural experience affiliate + retail"},{"name":"Chiapa de Corzo (UNESCO / Pueblo Mágico)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.viator.com/Chiapas-attractions/Sumidero-Canyon-National-Park/d5506-a14134","timing":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","commission":"paired with Sumidero day tour (DMC/affiliate, live)"},{"name":"Sumidero Canyon boat cruise","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.voyagemexique.info/en/sumidero-canyon/","hook":"2-hour open-boat cruise — life jackets, seated ride, weather-dependent; low risk with licensed operators from Chiapa de Corzo. Guided","si":"expedition","blurb":"2-hour open-boat cruise — life jackets, seated ride, weather-dependent; low risk with licensed operators from Chiapa de Corzo. Guided","commission":"guided boat tour commissionable (live); park/boat federal fee non-commissionable"},{"name":"Lagos de Montebello","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.voyagemexique.info/en/sumidero-canyon/","timing":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","commission":"guided long-day tour DMC (live) — keep to established tourist route near border"},{"name":"El Chiflón waterfalls","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.voyagemexique.info/en/sumidero-canyon/","si":"expedition","commission":"guided day tour DMC/affiliate (live) + entrance non-commissionable"},{"name":"El Arcotete / Rancho Nuevo","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://randomtrip.net/san-cristobal-de-las-casas-travel-guide-chiapas-mexico/","timing":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"[''Nov-Apr dry season'', ''Dia de Muertos '', ''Semana Santa '']","commission":"local guide/transfer affiliate + entrance (live)"},{"name":"Temazcal + boutique-casa spa evenings","si_tag":"romance","tier":"comfort","source":"http://www.casadelalmahotelboutiqueandspa.com/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"romance","when":"year-round","commission":"hotel + spa package direct/DMC (live)"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for — is the road dangerous?","a":"The connective road is the risk, not the city. Highway 199 between San Cristóbal and Palenque via Ocosingo has reported armed robberies (predominantly at night) plus periodic CNTE union blockades that usually cause only short delays. The rule is daytime-only overland travel with a vetted guide or private transfer, never a night self-drive; the city center itself is pedestrian-comfortable by day.","source":"aboutsancristobal.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What are San Juan Chamula and Zinacantán, and how do I visit respectfully?","a":"They are living Tzotzil Maya villages, 10 km out, and a guide is effectively mandatory. Chamula''s church is a pine-needle-floored space of Maya-Catholic fusion with ritual healings day and night and a strict no-photography rule inside; Zinacantán (99% Indigenous) is a backstrap-loom weaving town with a women''s co-op. Pay the community fees and follow a guide who knows the etiquette.","source":"wandersmiles.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What is there to do in the city itself?","a":"Walk the pedestrian andadores — Real de Guadalupe and the Andador Eclesiástico — between two hillside churches. The Templo de Santo Domingo has Chiapas''s most elaborate carved pink facade with a Tzotzil/Tzeltal textile market at its churchyard, and the Museo del Ámbar (in the ex-convent of La Merced) shows amber with 25-million-year-old inclusions, alongside a strong Chiapas-coffee and cacao café culture.","source":"randomtrip.net, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What is Sumidero Canyon, and is it worth it?","a":"Yes — it''s the region''s signature nature outing. A 2-hour open-boat cruise from the UNESCO colonial town of Chiapa de Corzo runs ~32 km beneath canyon walls up to ~1,000 m, past waterfalls and wildlife. It''s a low-risk daytime trip with licensed operators — life vests on, weather-dependent.","source":"voyagemexique.info, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is San Cristóbal a good base for a quiet, cultured couple''s trip?","a":"Yes — it''s cultured romance, not resort romance. At 2,200 m the highland evenings ask for a sweater; boutique colonial casas like Hotel Bö and Casa del Alma offer temazcal spa culture and courtyard dinners along cobblestone andadores. Come in the dry season (Nov–April), with crisp 18–24°C days, blue skies and minimal rain.","source":"climatestotravel.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Does the altitude affect visitors?","a":"Only mildly. At ~2,200 m some travelers feel light shortness of breath or a disturbed first night''s sleep, but it is not a serious altitude risk — hydrate and ease into exertion on day one. Drink bottled water only; dengue is a lowland concern (Palenque, the canyon), not the cool highland city.","source":"climatestotravel.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"San Cristóbal de las Casas, Mexico: Highland Chiapas, Maya Culture & Sumidero Canyon | TravelWell","search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en San Cristóbal de las Casas","Cañón del Sumidero","San Juan Chamula","Zinacantán tejido","Lagos de Montebello","El Chiflón cascadas","hoteles boutique San Cristóbal","mejor época para viajar a Chiapas","es seguro San Cristóbal de las Casas"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","freshness":"2026-07-07","primary_keyword":"San Cristóbal de las Casas"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Hotel Bö","tier":"design-luxury boutique (not global 5-star)","earning":"Fora/Virtuoso consortia commission where participating; else bedbank/OTA","mor":true},{"name":"Casa del Alma Hotel Boutique & Spa","tier":"upper-mid spa boutique","earning":"consortia/agency commission or bedbank","mor":true},{"name":"Hotel Na Bolom","tier":"mid heritage/character","earning":"direct/OTA thin commission, high narrative value","mor":true},{"name":"Private-DMC program (Plan South America / bespoke)","tier":"ultra ground handle incl. private charter SC<->Palenque ~40min","earning":"MoR on itinerary not bed","mor":true}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"San Cristóbal de las Casas, Mexico, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":16.737,"lng":-92.6376}}'::jsonb, 96),
  ('san-ignacio-belize', '10S', 'San Ignacio / Cayo, Belize', 'Belize', 'Belize''s inland adventure capital', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Belize', '{"expedition","culture","romance"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Base for Actun Tunichil Muknal (ATM) — a guided-only Maya sacrificial cave holding the calcified ''Crystal Maiden'' skeleton near San Ignacio, Cayo District.","Xunantunich''s El Castillo (~40 m) is Belize''s 2nd-tallest structure; reached by a hand-cranked Mopan River ferry ~20 min from town.","Caracol''s Caana pyramid (141 ft / 43 m) is Belize''s tallest structure; access via military-escorted convoy from Douglas D''Silva Forest Station (~9 am) due to Guatemala-border proximity.","Blancaneaux Lodge, a ~20-room hideaway in the Mountain Pine Ridge, was bought by Francis Ford Coppola in the early 1980s and opened to guests in 1993.","BZE (Belize International) to San Ignacio is a ~2-hour drive west on the Western/George Price Highway; the Cayo caves are accessible year-round."],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (verify)","hospital":"San Ignacio Community Hospital (local); trauma to Belize City (~2 hrs) or air-medical evac to Belize City / Guatemala City (verify)","book_enabled":true,"l3_disclosure":true,"state_dept_carveout":"only Southside Belize City restricted; Cayo open","stay_in_zone":true,"air_access_verified":"BZE -> San Ignacio ~2 hr drive, Western/George Price Highway; regional airstrip Maya Flats (verify)","guatemala_border_note":"Caracol requires military-escorted convoy; Xunantunich near border — disclose, verify current","malaria":"CDC: malaria a risk in SOME parts of Belize; treat mainland jungle as potential risk, advise travel-medicine consult","dengue":"present; mosquito-bite avoidance essential","vaccines":"Hepatitis A (all 1+), typhoid (rural/smaller-city) recommended","water":"bottled/treated only; avoid swimming in fresh unchlorinated water (leptospirosis) — ATM/cave-tubing are unavoidable-immersion guided activities"},"timing":{"curve_shape":"dry-season inland spike (cave/road passability), not beach-weather driven","peak":"Dec-Apr dry season; Dec-Jan crowd/price peak; Feb-Mar balanced sweet spot","green_season":"Jun-Nov wet; caves accessible year-round and especially evocative Jun-Oct at high water; rates drop","hurricane_overlay":"Jun-Nov; Sep-Oct highest risk; direct Belize landfalls historically infrequent","fire_date":"~2026-11-20 (primary, dry-season ramp); secondary pulse ~late May (green-season value)","sharpen_note":"season boundaries drift; confirm cave-tour operating status + road passability on live operator advisories before each fire date"},"jewels":[{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Actun Tunichil Muknal (ATM) — Crystal Maiden","tier":"comfort","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Actun_Tunichil_Muknal","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"licensed DMC / lodge tour desk (~$164 pp)"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Cave-tubing (Caves Branch / Cayo)","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.pacztours.net/","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"DMC day-tour + lodge bundle"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Barton Creek Cave (canoe-through)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.pacztours.net/","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Paddled by canoe through a river cave with Maya archaeological remains — guided only","si":"expedition","blurb":"Paddled by canoe through a river cave with Maya archaeological remains — guided only","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"licensed DMC tour"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Mountain Pine Ridge + Rio On Pools + Rio Frio Cave + Big Rock Falls","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/jungle-lodges-belize/","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"DMC 4x4 day tour / lodge-based"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Horseback riding (Macal/Mopan valleys)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://chaacreek.com/","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"lodge activity / DMC"},{"si_tag":"culture","name":"Xunantunich + El Castillo + hand-cranked ferry","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.nayawalk.com/belize/xunantunich/","hook":"The Classic Maya city sits near the Belize–Guatemala border","si":"culture","blurb":"The Classic Maya city sits near the Belize–Guatemala border","commission":"DMC half-day / lodge tour"},{"si_tag":"culture","name":"Caracol — Caana (Belize''s tallest structure)","tier":"premier","source":"https://trans-americas.com/caracol-archaeological-site-belize/","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Reached only by military-escorted convoy from the Douglas D''Silva Forest Station because of Guatemala-border proximity","si":"culture","blurb":"Reached only by military-escorted convoy from the Douglas D''Silva Forest Station because of Guatemala-border proximity","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"licensed DMC full-day + convoy logistics"},{"si_tag":"culture","name":"Cahal Pech (walking distance from town)","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.stleonardsbelize.com/belize-tours/xunantunich-cahal-pech-tour","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"self-guided fee / add-on guided walk"},{"si_tag":"culture","name":"Tikal day-trip (Guatemala)","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.pacztours.net/","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"licensed DMC full-day cross-border"},{"si_tag":"Romance & Nature","name":"Green Iguana Conservation Project","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.sanignaciobelize.com/green-iguana-conservation-project/","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Romance & Nature","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"in-town lodge activity / affiliate"},{"si_tag":"Romance & Nature","name":"Belize Botanic Gardens at du Plooy''s","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.sanignaciobelize.com/","si":"Romance & Nature","commission":"lodge stay / day visit / bedbank"},{"si_tag":"Romance & Nature","name":"Chaa Creek Butterfly Farm + Macal River canoe","tier":"comfort","source":"https://chaacreek.com/","timing":"Dec-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Romance & Nature","when":"Dec-Apr dry season","commission":"lodge stay + activity"},{"si_tag":"Romance & Nature","name":"Spanish Lookout (Mennonite community)","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/belize/western-belize/san-ignacio-cayo/attractions/green-iguana-conservation-project/a/poi-sig/460812/358218","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"Romance & Nature","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC add-on / self-drive"}],"faq":[{"q":"What is the ATM cave tour like, and do you need a guide?","a":"It is the apex Cayo adventure and it is guided-only by law — you cannot legally enter Actun Tunichil Muknal without a licensed operator. Expect a ~45-minute jungle trek with multiple river crossings, a swim into the cave mouth, wading a shallow underground river in total darkness, and tight climbs; ~3 hours inside. Cameras have been banned since a 2012 incident cracked a ~1,000-year-old skull.","source":"en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"How do you visit Caracol and Xunantunich?","a":"Differently. Caracol — whose Caana pyramid (141 ft/43 m) is Belize''s tallest structure — requires a military-escorted convoy from the Douglas D''Silva Forest Station (muster ~9 am, return ~2 pm) because it sits near the porous Guatemala border. Xunantunich is easier: a 20-minute drive and a hand-cranked Mopan River ferry to El Castillo, ~40 m and the country''s second-tallest structure.","source":"trans-americas.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is San Ignacio good for a honeymoon?","a":"Yes — for jungle romance rather than beach. The luxury lodge belt is world-class: Coppola''s Blancaneaux Lodge (~20 rooms, Mountain Pine Ridge waterfalls), the 500-acre Green Globe reserve at Chaa Creek (founded 1981, with butterfly farm, spa and Macal River canoeing), and Ka''ana''s plunge-pool villas. Plunge-pool casitas, canopy dinners and waterfall spas define the market.","source":"chaacreek.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Cayo?","a":"Water, wildlife and inland health, not urban crime. CDC advises avoiding swimming in fresh, unchlorinated water (leptospirosis), yet ATM and cave-tubing involve unavoidable river immersion, so treat them as guided-only informed-consent activities; high water after heavy rain periodically closes the caves. CDC also states malaria is a risk in some parts of Belize — treat the mainland jungle as potential risk and get a travel-medicine consult; dengue is present.","source":"wwwnc.cdc.gov, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is the ATM cave tour dangerous?","a":"It is physically demanding but safe as a licensed, guided activity — there is no legal or safe self-tour option. The tour requires \"good to very good\" fitness for river fordings, swimming into the cave, and tight passages and climbs in the upper chambers, with a minimum height of ~40 inches. Cave-tubing and Barton Creek Cave are likewise licensed-guide-required, with rising-water hazard after rain.","source":"chaacreek.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"San Ignacio & Cayo, Belize: ATM Cave, Xunantunich, Caracol & Jungle Lodges | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Belize''s inland adventure capital — swim into the Crystal Maiden''s cave, climb Caracol and Xunantunich, sleep in Coppola''s jungle hideaway. Guided-only cave tours, luxury eco-lodges, how to travel Cayo well.","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-06","search_language":"en","local_keywords":["San Ignacio Belize","Cayo District adventure","ATM cave tour","Actun Tunichil Muknal Crystal Maiden","Xunantunich hand-cranked ferry","Caracol military convoy","Blancaneaux Lodge Belize","cave tubing Belize","best jungle lodges San Ignacio","is Cayo Belize safe 2026"],"hreflang":["en","es-419 (optional)"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["expedition","Culture & Heritage (future)","romance"],"ultra":[{"name":"Blancaneaux Lodge","why":"~20-room Coppola hideaway, Mountain Pine Ridge, waterfall pools","earning_path":"Family Coppola Hideaways direct + consortia/Fora lane","mor":"direct-to-lodge","tier":"$$$$"},{"name":"Ka''ana Resort","why":"18 suites/villas, private plunge pools, boutique 17-acre estate","earning_path":"consortia/Fora + direct","mor":"direct","tier":"$$$-$$$$"},{"name":"The Lodge at Chaa Creek","why":"500-acre Green Globe reserve, Macal River, spa, villas","earning_path":"direct + advisor consortia","mor":"direct/AOR","tier":"$$$-$$$$"},{"name":"Gaïa Riverlodge","why":"Small Luxury Hotels of the World; 16 cabanas atop Five Sisters Falls, hydropowered","earning_path":"SLH channel + consortia","mor":"SLH/direct","tier":"premier"},{"name":"Table Rock Jungle Lodge","why":"intimate boutique Macal-riverfront cabañas","earning_path":"direct commission","mor":"direct","tier":"comfort"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"San Ignacio / Cayo, Belize, Belize"},"geo":{"lat":17.1598,"lng":-89.0714}}'::jsonb, 97),
